> cancel (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
cancel (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
  = -2x^2/3 - 2x/3 - 0.6666666667
  note: coefficients are printed rounded (numbers in expressions are doubles), so no exact check is printed
> expand 1/3*x + 2/3
  ucas: expand 1/3*x + 2/3
expand 0.3333333333x + 0.6666666667
  = x/3 + 0.6666666667
  note: coefficients are printed rounded (numbers in expressions are doubles), so no exact check is printed
> factor (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
  ucas: factor (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
factor (-4x^3 - 2x^2 - 2x + 2)/(6x - 3)
  = -2(x^2 + x + 1)/3
  holds where 2x - 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
